  "charts": [
    {
      "title": "Where the revenue grows, and what it earns",
      "note": "mark.point with a `size` channel on a scale.size: the area of each circle, not its radius, follows the value, so a product twice the revenue is a bubble twice the area. Big bubbles are drawn first, so small ones stay visible on top; an outline in the card color and some transparency separate the overlaps. The size key is a guide.legend on the size scale.",
